  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A homogeneous sphere floats with half its volume immersed in mercury <math> <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo></math>density <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>13</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>gm</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>c</mi><msup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math><math> <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo> </math> and the other half in oil <math> <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo></math>density <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>gm</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi>cc</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math><math> <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo> </math> in a vessel containing oil over mercury. What is the density of the&nbsp;material of the sphere in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>gm</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi>cc</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>?</p>\r"
